```Rule: Success after failures | MITRE T1078 Valid Accounts | Python rule: success_after_failures```
```Logic: a successful login from an IP that had >= 5 failed logins in the previous 10 minutes = likely compromised account```

```--- Linux SSH ---```
index=linux sourcetype=linux_secure ("Failed password" OR "Accepted")
| rex "(?<action>Failed|Accepted) \w+ for (invalid user )?(?<user>\S+) from (?<src_ip>\d{1,3}(\.\d{1,3}){3})"
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m count(eval(action="Failed")) AS recent_failures BY src_ip
| where action="Accepted" AND recent_failures >= 5
| table _time host src_ip user recent_failures

```--- Windows (4625 failures then 4624 success) ---```
index=wineventlog (EventCode=4625 OR EventCode=4624)
| sort 0 _time
| streamstats time_window=10m count(eval(EventCode=4625)) AS recent_failures BY src_ip
| where EventCode=4624 AND recent_failures >= 5
| table _time host src_ip user recent_failures
